G1106.b:
⟪γνώμη⟫, -ης, ἡ
(< γιγνώσκω), [in LXX: Da TH 2:15 (⁨דָּת⁩), Ps 82(83):3 (⁨סוֹד⁩), elsewhere, chiefly II Es, for ⁨טְעֵם⁩ ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪a means of knowing, a token⟫ (Theogn.).
⟪2.⟫ In Attic writers, ⟪the mind⟫, its operations and results (v. Edwards, Lex., App., A);
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪mind, understanding⟫;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪purpose, intention⟫: ⟦Acts 20:3|Ac 20:3⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ ⟪judgment, opinion⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 1:10|I Co 1:10⟧, ⟦Revelation 17:13|Re 17:13⟧;
	⟪(d)⟫ ⟪counsel, advice⟫: ⟦1 Corinthians 7:25|I Co 7:25⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:40|40⟧ ⟦2 Corinthians 8:10|II Co 8:10⟧, ⟦Philemon 1:14|Phm 14⟧;
	⟪(e)⟫ ⟪royal purpose, decree⟫ (as in Da, I and II Es): ⟦Revelation 17:17|Re 17:17⟧ (Cremer, 671). †

G1120.b:
*† ⟪γονυπετέω⟫, -ῶ (< γόνυ, πίπτω);
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to fall on the knees⟫: seq. ἔμπροσθεν, ⟦Matthew 27:29|Mt 27:29⟧.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to fall down before⟫ one: c. acc., ⟦Matthew 17:14|Mt 17:14⟧, ⟦Mark 1:40|Mk 1:40⟧, R, txt., ⟦Mark 10:17|10:17⟧.†

G1121.b:
⟪γράμμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< γράφω), [in LXX for ⁨סֵפֶר⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ ⟪that which is traced⟫ or ⟪drawn, a picture⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪that which is written⟫;
	⟪(1)⟫ ⟪a character, letter⟫: ⟦Galatians 6:11|Ga 6:11⟧;
	⟪(2)⟫ ⟪a writing, a written document⟫;
		⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a bill⟫ or ⟪account⟫: ⟦Luke 16:6|Lk 16:6⟧, ⟦Luke 16:7|7⟧;
		⟪(b)⟫ ⟪a letter⟫: ⟦Acts 28:21|Ac 28:21⟧;
		⟪(c)⟫ τὰ ἱερὰ γ., the sacred writings, i.e. the OT: ⟦2 Timothy 3:15|II Ti 3:15⟧ (so in Philo, Vit. Mos., iii, 39) ;
		⟪(d)⟫ τὸ γ., the letter, the written word as an external authority in contrast with the direct influence of the Spirit as manifested in the new Covenant: ⟦Romans 2:27|Ro 2:27⟧, ⟦Romans 2:29|29⟧ ⟦Romans 7:6|7:6⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:6|II Co 3:6⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 3:7|7⟧;
	⟪(3)⟫ τὰ γ., letters, i.e. learning: ⟦John 7:15|Jo 7:15⟧, ⟦Acts 26:24|Ac 26:24⟧. (In π. an illiterate person is very frequently referred to as γράμματα μὴ εἰδότης, and this "never means anything else than inability to write": MM, Exp., x; but v. also Cremer, 166; DCG, i, 202; ii, 584.) †

G1125.b:
⟪γράφω⟫, [in LXX chiefly for ⁨כּתב⁩ ];
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to scrape, graze⟫ (Hom.), and later (Hdt.) ⟪to sketch, draw⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to write⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ of forming or tracing letters on writing material: ⟦John 8:6|Jo 8:[6]⟧, ⟦Galatians 6:11|Ga 6:11⟧, ⟦2 Thessalonians 3:17|II Th 3:17⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ to express in writing, commit to writing, record: ⟦Luke 1:63|Lk 1:63⟧, ⟦John 19:21|Jo 19:21⟧, ⟦John 19:22|22⟧ ⟦Revelation 1:11|Re 1:11⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:19|19⟧ al.; of scripture as a standing authority (Deiss., BS, 112ff.), γέγραπται, it stands written (Luther), ⟦Matthew 4:4|Mt 4:4⟧, ⟦Mark 7:6|Mk 7:6⟧, ⟦Luke 4:8|Lk 4:8⟧, ⟦Romans 1:17|Ro 1:17⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:31|I Co 1:31⟧, al.; id. seq. ἐν, ⟦Mark 1:2|Mk 1:2⟧, ⟦Acts 1:20|Ac 1:20⟧, al.; c. acc., ⟪to write of⟫: ⟦John 1:46|Jo 1:46⟧, ⟦Romans 10:5|Ro 10:5⟧; seq. περί, ⟦Matthew 26:24|Mt 26:24⟧, ⟦Mark 14:21|Mk 14:21⟧, ⟦John 5:46|Jo 5:46⟧; al.; c. dat. (WM, §31, 4), ⟦Luke 18:31|Lk 18:31⟧; id. seq. ἵνα (M, Pr., 207f.), ⟦Mark 12:19|Mk 12:19⟧, ⟦Luke 20:28|Lk 20:28⟧; κατὰ τ. γεγραμμένον, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:13|II Co 4:13⟧; γεγραμμένον ἐστί, ⟦John 2:17|Jo 2:17⟧; ἐγράφη, ⟦Romans 4:24|Ro 4:24⟧; ἐπ’ αὐτῷ γεγραμμένα, ⟦John 12:16|Jo 12:16⟧;
	⟪(c)⟫ of writing directions or information, c. dat. pers.: ⟦Romans 15:15|Ro 15:15⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 7:12|II Co 7:12⟧, al.;
	⟪(d)⟫ of that which contains the record or message: βιβλίον, ⟦Mark 10:4|Mk 10:4⟧, ⟦John 21:25|Jo 21:25⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:1|Re 5:1⟧; τίτλον, ⟦John 19:19|Jo 19:19⟧; ἐπιστολήν, ⟦Acts 23:25|Ac 23:25⟧; ἐντολήν, ⟦Mark 10:5|Mk 10:5⟧ (cf. ἀπο-, ἐγ-, ἐπι-, κατα-, προ-).

G1140.b:
⟪δαιμόνιον⟫, -ου, τό
(neut. of δαιμόνιος, -α, -ον, divine), [in LXX (so also in π; v. MM, Exp., x) for ⁨שֵׁד⁩, ⁨אֱלִיל⁩, (freq. in Tob) ;]
⟪1.⟫ as in cl.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪the Divine power, Deity⟫ (Hdt., Plat., al.);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪an inferior divinity, deity⟫ or ⟪demon⟫ (as in magical π, Deiss., BS, 281; MM, Exp., x): ξένα δ., ⟦Acts 17:18|Ac 17:18⟧.
⟪2.⟫ (a) in OT, heathen deities, false gods (e.g. ⟦Deuteronomy 32:17|De 32:17⟧, Ps 95 (96):5);
⟪(b)⟫ in NT, ⟪evil spirits, demons⟫: θύουσιν δαιμονίοις, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:20|I Co 10:20⟧; διδασκαλίαι δαιμονίων, ⟦1 Timothy 4:1|I Ti 4:1⟧; προσκυνεῖν τὰ δ., ⟦Revelation 9:20|Re 9:20⟧; ἄρχων τῶν δ., ⟦Matthew 9:34|Mt 9:34⟧; especially (syn. with πνεῦμα ἀκάθαρτον) as operating upon and "possessing" (of. δαιμονίζομαι) men: ⟦Matthew 11:18|Mt 11:18⟧, et al.; εἰσέρχεσθαι δ. εἰς. . ., ⟦Luke 8:30|Lk 8:30⟧; δ. ἔχειν, ⟦Luke 4:33|Lk 4:33⟧; δ. ἐκβάλλειν, ⟦Matthew 7:22|Mt 7:22⟧ In the phrase πνεῦμα δαιμονίου ἀκαθάρτου, ⟦Luke 4:33|Lk 4:33⟧, the wider cl. usage (1. b) is recognised, ἀκ. being elsewhere in NT, the epithet of πν., and δ. = πν. ἀκ. (v. ICC, in l; Cremer, 168)

G1161.b:
⟪δέ⟫ (before vowels δ’; on the general neglect of the elision in NT, v. WH, App., 146; Tdf., Pr., 96), post-positive conjunctive particle;
⟪1.⟫ copulative, ⟪but, in the next place, and, now⟫ (Abbott, JG, 104): ⟦Matthew 1:2|Mt 1:2⟧ff., ⟦2 Corinthians 6:15|II Co 6:15⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 6:16|16⟧, ⟦2 Peter 1:5|II Pe 1:5-7⟧; in repetition for emphasis, ⟦Romans 3:21|Ro 3:21⟧, ⟦Romans 3:22|22⟧, ⟦Romans 9:30|9:30⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 2:6|I Co 2:6⟧, ⟦Galatians 2:2|Ga 2:2⟧, ⟦Philippians 2:8|Phl 2:8⟧; in transition to something new, ⟦Matthew 1:18|Mt 1:18⟧ ⟦Matthew 2:19|2:19⟧, ⟦Luke 13:1|Lk 13:1⟧, ⟦John 7:14|Jo 7:14⟧, ⟦Acts 6:1|Ac 6:1⟧, ⟦Romans 8:28|Ro 8:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 7:1|I Co 7:1⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 8:1|8:1⟧, al.; in explanatory parenthesis or addition, ⟦John 3:19|Jo 3:19⟧, ⟦Romans 5:8|Ro 5:8⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:12|I Co 1:12⟧, ⟦Ephesians 2:4|Eph 2:4⟧ ⟦Ephesians 5:32|5:32⟧, al.; ὡς δέ, ⟦John 2:9|Jo 2:9⟧; καὶ . . . δέ, but also, ⟦Matthew 10:18|Mt 10:18⟧, ⟦Luke 1:76|Lk 1:76⟧, ⟦John 6:51|Jo 6:51⟧, ⟦Romans 11:23|Ro 11:23⟧, al.; καὶ ἐὰν δέ, ⟪yea even if⟫, ⟦John 8:16|Jo 8:16⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Adversative, ⟪but, on the other hand⟫, prop., answering to a foregoing μέν (q.v.), and distinguishing a word or clause from one preceding (in NT most freq. without μέν; Bl., §77, 12): ἐὰν δέ, ⟦Matthew 6:14|Mt 6:14⟧, ⟦Matthew 6:23|23⟧, al.; ἐγὼ (σὺ, etc.) δέ, ⟦Matthew 5:22|Mt 5:22⟧ ⟦Matthew 6:6|6:6⟧, ⟦Mark 8:29|Mk 8:29⟧, al.; ὁ δέ, αὐτὸς δέ, ⟦Mark 1:45|Mk 1:45⟧, ⟦Luke 4:40|Lk 4:40⟧, al.; after a negation, ⟦Matthew 6:19|Mt 6:19⟧, ⟦Matthew 6:20|20⟧, ⟦Romans 3:4|Ro 3:4⟧, ⟦1 Thessalonians 5:21|I Th 5:21⟧, al.

G1166.b:
⟪δείκνυμι⟫, δεικνύω (v. Bl., § 23, 1; Veitch, s.v.),
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨רָאָה⁩ hi. ;] ⟪to show⟫, c. acc rei (pers.), dat. pers.;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to show, exhibit⟫: ⟦Matthew 4:8|Mt 4:8⟧ ⟦Matthew 8:4|8:4⟧, ⟦Mark 1:44|Mk 1:44⟧ ⟦Mark 14:15|14:15⟧, ⟦Luke 4:5|Lk 4:5⟧ ⟦Luke 5:14|5:14⟧ ⟦Luke 20:24|20:24⟧ ⟦Luke 22:12|22:12⟧ ⟦Luke 24:40|24:40⟧, ⟦John 2:18|Jo 2:18⟧ ⟦John 5:20|5:20⟧ ⟦John 10:32|10:32⟧ ⟦John 20:20|20:20⟧, ⟦Acts 7:3|Ac 7:3⟧ (LXX), ⟦1 Timothy 6:15|I Ti 6:15⟧, ⟦Revelation 17:1|Re 17:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 21:9|21:9⟧, ⟦Revelation 21:10|10⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:1|22:1⟧, ⟦Revelation 22:8|8⟧, pass., ⟦Hebrews 8:5|He 8:5⟧ (LXX);
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to make known⟫: ⟦Matthew 16:21|Mt 16:21⟧, ⟦John 14:8|Jo 14:8, 9⟧, ⟦Acts 10:28|Ac 10:28⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 12:31|I Co 12:31⟧, ⟦Revelation 1:1|Re 1:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 4:1|4:1⟧ ⟦Revelation 22:6|22:6⟧;
⟪(c)⟫ ⟪to prove⟫: ⟦James 2:18|Ja 2:18⟧ ⟦James 3:13|3:13⟧.†

G1175.b:
*† ⟪δεισιδαιμονία⟫, -ας, ἡ
(< δεισιδαίμων, q.v.);
⟪1.⟫ ⟪fear of the gods⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪piety, religion⟫;
⟪(b)⟫ ⟪superstition⟫.
⟪2.⟫ Objectively, ⟪a religion⟫: ⟦Acts 25:19|Ac 25:19⟧ (Cremer, 72, 682).†

G1189.b:
⟪δέομαι⟫
(mid. of δέω, II, q.v., as depon.) [in LXX for ⁨חנן⁩, etc. ;] ⟪to want for oneself⟫;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪to want, need⟫:
	⟪(a)⟫ absol.;
	⟪(b)⟫ c. gen.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to beg, request, beseech, pray⟫;
	⟪(i)⟫ in general: absol., ⟦Acts 26:3|Ac 26:3⟧, WH; c. gen. pers., ⟦Luke 5:12|Lk 5:12⟧ ⟦Luke 8:28|8:28⟧, ⟦Luke 8:38|38⟧ (ἐδεῖτο; T, ἐδέετο, cf. Veitch, s.v. δέω) ⟦Luke 9:38|9:38⟧, ⟦Acts 8:34|Ac 8:34⟧ ⟦Acts 21:39|21:39⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 5:20|II Co 5:20⟧, ⟦Galatians 4:12|Ga 4:12⟧; seq. ἵνα, ⟦Luke 9:40|Lk 9:40⟧; seq. τό, c. inf., ⟦2 Corinthians 10:2|II Co 10:2⟧; c. gen. pers. et rei, ⟦2 Corinthians 8:4|II Co 8:4⟧;
	⟪(ii)⟫ of prayer to God: absol., ⟦Acts 4:31|Ac 4:31⟧; seq. εἴ πως, ⟦Romans 1:10|Ro 1:10⟧; ἵνα, ⟦Luke 21:36|Lk 21:36⟧ ⟦Luke 22:32|22:32⟧; εἰς τό, ⟦1 Thessalonians 3:10|I Th 3:10⟧; ὑπὲρ ἐμοῦ πρὸς τ. κύριον, ὅπως, ⟦Acts 8:24|Ac 8:24⟧; c. gen., τοῦ κυρίου, ὅπως, ⟦Matthew 9:38|Mt 9:38⟧, ⟦Luke 10:2|Lk 10:2⟧; τοῦ Θεοῦ, ⟦Acts 10:2|Ac 10:2⟧; seq. εἰ ἄρα, ⟦Acts 8:22|Ac 8:22⟧.†
SYN.: αἰτέω, and cf. δέησις.
